                        "form": "швейца́рах"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1c90e675-6366-307a-8119-5c23061e2b13",
                        "entry_id": "4787fa60-2ae0-307b-86ae-8e2e71a38014",
                        "glosses": [
                            "одетый в униформу привратник в богатом доме или в учреждении"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "00ae167b-044e-413a-8a43-8c7f3610b4a8",
                                "sense_id": "1c90e675-6366-307a-8119-5c23061e2b13",
                                "text": "― Бонжур, месье, ― приветливо сказал швейцар у входа."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6236ef47-e5da-4757-947a-9e1de75fd695",
                                "sense_id": "1c90e675-6366-307a-8119-5c23061e2b13",
                                "text": "Мы много времени проводили в Союзгосцирке и часто заходили в «Берлин» выпить, перекусить. Нас все знали в лицо, и проблем попасть в ресторан не бывало, хотя в те годы на дверях гостиниц и ресторанов «Интуриста», даже пустовавших, вывешивали табличку «Мест нет» и людей «с улицы» не пускали. Однажды, как-то зимой, перебегаем мы из Союзгосцирка в «Берлин» ― стучу, прошу открыть двери, но незнакомый швейцар качает головой в фуражке, мол, не пущу."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "711b64a3-0278-33aa-804b-afb13add976e",
                        "entry_id": "4787fa60-2ae0-307b-86ae-8e2e71a38014",
                        "glosses": [
                            "устар. то же, что швейцарец"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c1973d06-292e-4482-9169-a64a2bf340fc",
                                "sense_id": "711b64a3-0278-33aa-804b-afb13add976e",
                                "text": "В клубе были и приверженцы Бонапарта — французы, эльзасцы, швейцары."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0aa0196f-216b-4126-b751-429e05004f3b",
                        "source_entry_id": "4787fa60-2ae0-307b-86ae-8e2e71a38014",
                        "target_lang_word": "porter",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "porter",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "99ca2e28-00cc-3b5f-a338-9df343bb1b3e",
                                        "entry_id": "20c8987a-0428-389b-963d-9d24c1d50f65",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person who carries luggage and related objects."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "896fceb8-da75-4cb2-a95b-ef440662b0c7",
                                                "sense_id": "99ca2e28-00cc-3b5f-a338-9df343bb1b3e",
                                                "text": "By the time I reached the train station I was exhausted, but fortunately there was a porter waiting."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "159054e4-0ac2-4049-9a6f-c7234646d20d",
                                                "sense_id": "99ca2e28-00cc-3b5f-a338-9df343bb1b3e",
                                                "text": "Achilles! a drayman, a porter, a very camel."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "11df132d-7075-48b8-b8a5-694a0b671866",
                                                "sense_id": "99ca2e28-00cc-3b5f-a338-9df343bb1b3e",
                                                "text": "the unsmotherable delight of all the porters and by - standers"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dbe6827c-493c-4dc2-8051-f04516057e30",
                                                "sense_id": "99ca2e28-00cc-3b5f-a338-9df343bb1b3e",
                                                "text": "The man who carries your luggage at the station is a \"red cap\", not a porter. The Canadian porter is the man who makes up the beds in the sleeping cars."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b1544956-b6d6-429d-9d7e-20f45d1d9fb6",
                                                "sense_id": "99ca2e28-00cc-3b5f-a338-9df343bb1b3e",
                                                "text": "As soon as we had come to a stand in Kamina Station, a swarm of porters pushed their way into the compartment to get my luggage. I selected one, and ordered the others out, and then detrained."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "144338c0-84b6-4a42-993c-bff9b62ba8d9",
                                                "sense_id": "99ca2e28-00cc-3b5f-a338-9df343bb1b3e",
                                                "text": "Tips were an important part of porters' income, and at Christmas passengers felt there was extra pressure to give them - despite some perceiving the level of service to be poor."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9aab3f9f-1a58-3584-ab35-0ac713de9a48",
                                        "entry_id": "20c8987a-0428-389b-963d-9d24c1d50f65",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An ant having the specialized role of carrying."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2fc110f0-0fc2-369f-8c2a-32755c704a0f",
                                        "entry_id": "20c8987a-0428-389b-963d-9d24c1d50f65",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One who ports software (makes it usable on another platform)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "85b9c1f6-a72c-4521-8bdb-be5c8ad74439",
                                                "sense_id": "2fc110f0-0fc2-369f-8c2a-32755c704a0f",
                                                "text": "[…] useful only if you are a Perl porter or implementor and you want to check the efficiency of the hashing algorithm."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "porter",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c37702d3-da5b-385e-9cbd-d47abfbafe22",
                                        "entry_id": "bab496e7-855b-37bb-9f49-f46b401151e5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person in control of the entrance to a building."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9161ef74-4af8-3fd8-8724-d77816f48d7f",
                                        "entry_id": "bab496e7-855b-37bb-9f49-f46b401151e5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An employee who clears and cleans tables and puts bowling balls away."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0acfee9a-2927-378c-8acf-b0958a4aaa46",
                                        "entry_id": "bab496e7-855b-37bb-9f49-f46b401151e5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A strong, dark ale, originally favored by porters (etymology 1, sense 1), similar to a stout but less strong."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "05c39e16-cde7-3d5b-9139-495d5dfe5658",
                                        "entry_id": "bab496e7-855b-37bb-9f49-f46b401151e5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Stout (malt brew)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Ireland",
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "787a2b7f-9f48-4c2d-bb86-4a73ee8c6e80",
                                                "sense_id": "05c39e16-cde7-3d5b-9139-495d5dfe5658",
                                                "text": "‘Here, Pat, give us a g.p., like a good fellow.’ The curate brought him a glass of plain porter. The man drank it at a gulp and asked for a caraway seed."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
